# M1B Mechanical Review Component Specification

Status: Prepared source/data; combined preseal and actual execution pending

Implemented Through: Not applicable

Purpose: Bind independent logical-ownership, checkpoint, type and loaded-counterproof mechanisms without promoting source inspection or author evidence into target acceptance.

## Normative Language

MUST, MUST NOT, SHOULD and MAY identify requirements of this review component,
not new virtual-bash product APIs. Implementation-defined choices MUST be stated
in the committed composition before execution.

## Problem Statement

The candidate is source `fca6f81d2d96db2bbceabf3247cd57ffe240bde6`, evidence
`897e5141b034b59501f576a259d5ea1e7e2673c6`, derived-only tree
`23074ef0c443ca618c4f26204b5f3d2274b86895`. The full910 artifact is
`cc0e75c2d0d12f713f0458e608ddeae157cf3432b4e0b48277a329a98115aa1a`.
SOURCE-BINDINGS and PACKAGE-MAP distinguish selected source, whole Git identities,
and author-built output. Package count alone is not composition evidence.

S01's source correction protects the first allocation before the second.
Independent exceptional-path execution remains UNRUN. S02's packed-writer versus
read-side error provenance remains an unexecuted concern. An abstract observer
qualifier is not an M1B native codec adapter.

## Goals and Non-Goals

The component MUST retain all32 resource rows and108 variants, including masks,
missing mechanisms and source-only obligations. Private methods MUST be labeled
private mechanical observations, not stock commands or public cap success.

The component MUST NOT change production files, fixed limits, private counters,
budgets, refunds, public APIs or author histories. Its isolated counter mutant
omits release accounting only as a separately admitted diagnostic executable.
It MUST NOT be admitted to ordinary semantic cases. No native Git or external
engine is part of this component.

## Boundary and Authority

The committed runner ABI is `de95161c9de136852884d054612dad1b8ec716e5`.
The component exports `runCase(api, caseId)` and uses only its fixed facilities.
It MUST NOT spawn a child or invent tool, observer or fixture APIs.

S is independently compiled selected source. M is the whole offline package
after physical relocation. Author output MUST NOT be called independently built.
Internal direct-module imports MUST NOT be described as public export integration.
The absent root Git export remains PUBLIC_EXPORT_GAP.

Selected source and emitted spans, hashes, modes and full package maps are DATA.
Before any mutant load the runner MUST materialize an isolated full910 projection,
authenticate its exact map and loaded bytes, and reject all undeclared paths.
Each pristine, mutant and restore case MUST have a new process/import namespace.
Source transform correspondence is not a newly compiled artifact. Maps and
declarations in diagnostic projections stay unchanged, explicitly not proof that
those maps describe the transformed instruction locations.

## Observation Contracts

### Logical ownership

S01 uses the actual private emitted `PackCatalogue.index` method and actual
`Session.allocate`, `reserve`, `unreserve` and `release` methods. The independent
N2/L1 fixture is index-parser data, not a valid compressed-pack workflow. Session
has a minimal host context for the inspected private paths; it is not a complete
public CommandContext or FS adapter.

Per-instance wrappers MUST delegate original receiver, arguments and return or
thrown value unchanged except at the one declared fail site. Error, null and
undefined injection MUST compare the actual thrown reference/value locally.
Allocation failure injection wraps Buffer.alloc only during the synchronous
selected allocate call. Its exact descriptor MUST be restored before any await.
Normal operation MUST never call a fabricated budget or lower a cap.

The release observer MUST record actual delegated unreserve calls. The counter
mutant MUST run the witness and make the pristine predicate false; a hash denial,
crash, timeout or absent injection MUST NOT count as a loaded kill. Reversion
and restoration have separate executions and source identities. A logical owner
left by a deliberate mutant is not a measured native memory leak or RSS claim.

### Checkpoints and inheritance

CRC/hash/replay cases abort at explicit actual Session.step calls. They MUST
report private deterministic checkpoint behavior, not native scheduling latency,
preemption or full public invocation cancellation. Delta inheritance cases use
one-byte data and verify inherited type and result bytes only; they MUST NOT claim
that this byte is a valid parsed tree, commit or tag for a complete Git query.

### Native codec and cleanup

The current M1B adapter is UNQUALIFIED. ADAPTER-CRITERIA binds the packed codec
and selected OutputOperation source separately. A createInflate factory facade
cannot directly observe lexical `written`. Writer-only close hooks MUST NOT
label every close listener as writer ownership. A source-linked conditional join
MUST stay distinct from a directly observed promise or native retirement fact.

Future qualification MUST preserve actual receiver/arguments/chunks/callbacks,
iterator return and error identity, distinct writer/reader/cleanup roles, one
invocation's hook/no-hook paths, and actual Shell invocation boundaries. Unknown
owned cleanup or retirement MUST STOP further admission. No hard host-preemption
or one-live-codec assertion follows from old289/288 notification counts.

S02's reader may reject before the normal `await written`; its finally joins
written with rejection suppression. Caller abortion and operation cancellation
checks precede codec-error mapping. This static ordering MUST NOT be substituted
for an observation proving the primary writer reason survives every read-side
failure. Caller reason, command nonzero, escaping rejection and cleanup failure
MUST remain distinct.

## Types and Diagnostic Rules

The five committed `.mts.data` files MUST be materialized only at the exact paths
and token substitutions in TYPES. The runner MUST use the pinned standalone
strict NodeNext compiler closure, without ambient config, NODE_PATH or installs.
Only declared diagnostic code, file, line, column and exact message are allowed.
Unknown or extra output MUST fail. All stdout/stderr/status/signal/time/reap and
loaded declaration provenance MUST be captured before the worker asserts.

The ABI requires every nonzero child to remain aggregate FAIL. Therefore the
four expected-negative fixtures per layout can produce matched diagnostic
counterproof but MUST NOT be called passing compiler processes. This component
does not introduce an exception to obtain a green aggregate.

## Bounds and Failure Model

COSTS specifies18 worker starts plus10 compiler starts, not18 total processes.
All nested compiler time is inside its wrapper's30s window. Two ordinary batches
share30s each across all16 private cases; no per-case or per-layout renewal is
permitted. The18 windows total540s inside root's single120min origin including
cleanup. Root's168 children/peak4/256MiB capture/1GiB working ceilings remain
unchanged. The coordinator MUST reconcile shared costs before combined preseal.

Capture acknowledgement MUST precede assertions. Failed raw capture, unexpected
child status, unguarded imports or unknown cleanup MUST NOT be hidden by successful
later commands. PREP01 and PREP02 remain preparation failures. No target, compiler,
control, observer or loader execution occurred in this preparation.

## Test and Validation Matrix

| Obligation | Prepared mechanism | Current evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Selected source282/full package910/907 unchanged | Exact Git/data inventories | STATIC authenticated, not build proof |
| S01 fail sites/ownership |9 private cases per S/M; isolated reversion triplet | UNRUN |
| Release accounting | Loaded pristine/omission/restoration triplet | UNRUN |
| CRC/hash/replay checkpoint abort |3 private cases per S/M | UNRUN |
| Nonblob inheritance metadata |4 private cases per S/M | UNRUN, not full parsed objects |
| Direct declaration types |5 fixtures per S/M,10 compiler requests | UNRUN;8 expected nonzero remain aggregate FAIL |
| CRC/OID/depth mutants | Exact source/emitted transform data | Actor/peer fixture binding pending |
|32 resource rows/108 variants | Exact per-ID disposition and source sites | No full row or variant pass |
| M1B codec and cleanup | Distinct qualification criteria | UNQUALIFIED, source-only observations |

## Conformance Criteria

This packet is a bounded component handoff, not launch approval or full coverage.
Conformance requires authenticated active closure, root's complete combined
preseal and route, exact fixture/mutant integration, and actual captured evidence
meeting the criteria above. Any unmet criterion MUST remain UNRUN, SOURCE_ONLY,
UNQUALIFIED or FAIL as applicable; it MUST NOT become an implicit pass.

